# netsurf: binary request bodies for XMLHttpRequest and fetch(), XHR
# responseType arraybuffer / blob / json (patch 256)
# Generated 2026-10-12
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 255)
#
# Found running hCaptcha live in the simulator (claude.ai's email sign-in,
# now that WebAssembly runs hsw, patch 254): its getcaptcha POST is a
# msgpack body of about 32 KB, NULs and all, sent from a Uint8Array with
# Content-Type application/octet-stream, and its answer is binary too.
#
#  - Requests: __xhrNativeSend took the body with JS_ToCString, so a
#    Uint8Array went out as "146,218,2,..." (api.hcaptcha.com: 415); fetch()
#    UTF-8 decoded byte bodies first, which mangles binary; and the fetch
#    layer copied the body with strdup, cutting it at the first NUL. Now an
#    ArrayBuffer, a typed array or a Blob is sent as its exact bytes (a
#    DataView through a Uint8Array, a typed Blob with its type), through
#    fetch_start_body (content/fetch.c): the length rides on struct fetch
#    for the fetcher's setup, and curl gets CURLOPT_POSTFIELDSIZE (reset to
#    -1 for every other body: handles are reused). Bytes with no type of
#    their own go without one, not with curl's default
#    application/x-www-form-urlencoded. Blob bytes come from the bridge's
#    native Blob (macsurf_qjs_blob_bytes).
#  - Responses: XHR's response was always the body as a C string (cut at
#    the first NUL, UTF-8 decoded). responseType "arraybuffer" and "blob"
#    now get the exact bytes (a Blob typed by Content-Type), "json" the
#    parsed value (null if it does not parse), and text is no longer cut at
#    a NUL. (fetch() responses were already byte-exact, patch 132.)
#
# hCaptcha still does not sign anyone in: getcaptcha now answers
# {"c":<a new hsw request>,"success":false,"error-codes":[]} where Chromium
# gets its 4 KB encrypted challenge -- hsw fingerprints about 25 APIs this
# engine lacks (WebGL, OfflineAudioContext, NavigatorUAData, Permissions,
# MediaDevices, ...) under a Chrome 140 user agent. See
# docs/wasm-hcaptcha-measurement.md, step 3.
#
# Gate: testpages/pages/JS-fetch-body.html grows checks 5-12 (Uint8Array,
# ArrayBuffer with its type, DataView window, typed Blob both ways,
# responseType json, fetch with a Uint8Array and a Blob; 300 bytes covering
# every value), 12/12 over http and https (Chromium 12/12; the build before
# this patch 4/12).
